Problem at mobile/tablet: the portrait (aside) appears BELOW the CTA row and hero is mostly empty? At 390: h1 y=181, cta y=445, aside y=527, hero ends 806. So order:-1 didn't put portrait first?? Because `.portrait{order:-1}` applies to the figure inside `.hero__aside`, not the aside itself. Right. So aside stays second and portrait order within aside irrelevant. That's why hero is 741: status+h1+tagline+meta+cta (445+48) then aside 237 below → looks odd: portrait after CTA. Also large empty right space next to name.

Fix: at <=900, `order:-1` on `.hero__aside`, and layout: maybe place portrait at top-left small, then name. That yields hero: portrait 237 + gap 34 + left 378 = 649 + padding ~ 741. Still tall. Better mobile design: put portrait to the side of the h1 (name row) rather than a full block. E.g. at mobile, `.hero__aside` becomes row with portrait small (112px) and name-note hidden; place it after h1? Design idea: name giant full width, then a row with small portrait at left and tagline to right? At 390 tagline needs width.

Simplest strong mobile composition:
- status pill
- h1
- small portrait (110px) floating right beside tagline? Could use grid: `.hero__left` after h1? Not easy without markup changes.

